    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.icons\n\n### Description\n\nHi~ 👋🏻 \r\n\r\nI've just found some plugins (for my case, `nvim-linefly`) seem to use `vim.g.nvim_web_devicons` to detect the use of icons.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/bluz71/nvim-linefly/blob/20102924d734a8f3ca760575b2b9a544efcf8dd3/lua/linefly/file.lua#L12\r\n\r\nDoes it make sense to set `vim.g.nvim_web_devicons = 1` in `mock_nvim_web_devicons()`?\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/nvim-tree/nvim-web-devicons/blob/e73d2774d12d0ecf9e05578d692ba1ea50508cf2/plugin/nvim-web-devicons.vim#L7\r\n",
